WEBVTT

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Thursday the twenty-sixth. Everyone on? I've got seven little boxes and about three ceilings.</v>

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:18.309
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, here. Honestly, the traffic on the ring road. Barely moved for twenty minutes.</v>

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:23.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>You're moving now, though. Your camera's making me seasick.</v>

00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:31.570
<v Grace Liu>Sorry! There. Was hoping to get out walking at the weekend, but the weather looks absolutely grim. Anyone got better plans?</v>

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.679
<v David Whitfield>Staying indoors. Been training for it all winter.</v>

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:44.490
<v Grace Liu>Oh, and there's a birthday cake in the office. Before we get buried in all this.</v>

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:48.539
<v Jamie Brennan>Finally, a useful production update.</v>

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:55.450
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cake duly noted. Finished stuff first, then what we're actually taking on.</v>

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:03.000
<v Grace Liu>We tested the HV switchboard yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done, not something for today's list.</v>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.700
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, that's the closed item. Nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:14.560
<v David Whitfield>And I finished the repair on the wrapper last night. That repair's complete.</v>

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. But we've got a jam on it this morning. Separate from what you repaired?</v>

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:28.200
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, separate. The repaired bit's fine. It's the jam and the sensor state we're talking about now.</v>

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:35.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the wrapper. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:41.519
<v David Whitfield>Cheers, Saz. Just wanted it clear we weren't reopening last night's repair.</v>

00:01:42.489 --> 00:01:45.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. New jam, separate job. I've got it.</v>

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:54.689
<v Grace Liu>While we're saying wrapper — I noticed the stretch wrapper was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down. Just an observation.</v>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>Different thing from this jam, then? Don't want those getting muddled.</v>

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.280
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. It settled down, no new job coming out of that.</v>

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:11.400
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same sort of thing from me: heard a slight rattle from the GT2 water valve. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only, not an extra job for you.</v>

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:23.240
<v Priya Raman>I'm still blocked on the turbine one gas valve. Can't get to it until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.150
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that stays blocked. We're not pretending it's booked in.</v>

00:02:28.719 --> 00:02:34.669
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 1 TCU. Same position as before.</v>

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery hiding in the paperwork, either.</v>

00:02:40.139 --> 00:02:43.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. That's a blocker update, not a fresh delivery promise.</v>

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.740
<v Jamie Brennan>Um, on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve, I'll replace the seals. That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie. Replacement of the seals on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve is yours, then.</v>

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:03.819
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll do that. Definitely one for the actual work list, not the closed stuff.</v>

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:13.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide Adeyemi, can you do the pre-use checks on the forklifts by end of day? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:24.629
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, no, I can't take that as well. I haven't got the capacity, and I don't want to say yes and leave them sitting there.</v>

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:35.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Tom, can you take the pre-use checks on the forklifts instead? Same thing: by end of day, but that's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll take them. Pre-use checks on the forklifts first for me, done by end of day.</v>

00:03:44.379 --> 00:03:51.030
<v Grace Liu>And obviously they don't go into use unchecked. End of day isn't permission to run them before the checks.</v>

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:54.360
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, absolutely. That's why I'm putting them first.</v>

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:01.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you also chase the purchase order for the wrapper today? Low priority, that one.</v>

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:07.560
<v Tomasz Nowak>The purchase order, yeah? Not the unconfirmed delivery we were just talking about?</v>

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:15.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, just chase the purchase order for the wrapper. Separate from the line 1 TCU blocker. Today, low priority.</v>

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:21.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Got you. I'll chase the purchase order for the wrapper today, lower down than the forklifts.</v>

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:29.350
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, two different bits of paperwork. Easy enough to cross the wires with all these names.</v>

00:04:30.509 --> 00:04:36.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one. Olumide Adeyemi, can you schedule downtime for line one with production first thing tomorrow? Fairly important.</v>

00:04:38.339 --> 00:04:45.339
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can't own that one either, sorry. Same capacity problem. Better to hand it over than have me half agree.</v>

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:53.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Grace, can you take that instead — schedule downtime for line one with production first thing tomorrow? It's fairly important.</v>

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:02.100
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll take it. I'll schedule downtime for line one with production first thing tomorrow. Fairly important, understood.</v>

00:05:04.329 --> 00:05:12.029
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talking over you there — first thing tomorrow is when you're doing the scheduling, not saying the line's going down then?</v>

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:19.089
<v Grace Liu>Correct. That's when I'll do the scheduling with production. We haven't agreed an actual downtime slot here.</v>

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:27.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you run the monthly fire alarm test first thing tomorrow? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:36.480
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yes, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test first thing tomorrow. Not an urgent one for today, understood.</v>

00:05:36.959 --> 00:05:39.410
<v Grace Liu>Monthly already. February's about six minutes long.</v>

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>Still manages to fit a full month's paperwork in, somehow.</v>

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:51.100
<v Jamie Brennan>One more from me. I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the water booster after lunch.</v>

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:56.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Jamie Brennan. Water booster lock-out tag-out sign-off, after lunch — you've got that.</v>

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.490
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, that's mine. After lunch.</v>

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:05.050
<v Priya Raman>Just keeping the wording straight — sign-off, not us agreeing a restart on this call.</v>

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:10.300
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. I'm taking the lock-out tag-out sign-off, not adding a restart.</v>

00:06:12.519 --> 00:06:19.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. For me, the wrapper jam and sensors are the drop-everything job. Tom's got the production hold-up first on his side.</v>

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:27.279
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep. Forklifts first, by end of day. Purchase order for the wrapper today as well, but low priority.</v>

00:06:29.009 --> 00:06:35.310
<v Grace Liu>And I've got scheduling with production for line one first thing tomorrow. Nothing extra from the warm-running observation.</v>

00:06:36.019 --> 00:06:40.569
<v Tomasz Nowak>Monthly fire alarm test first thing tomorrow for me as well. That's clear.</v>

00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:46.670
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the line 1 TCU delivery is still unconfirmed. No change on that during this call.</v>

00:06:47.279 --> 00:06:53.930
<v Priya Raman>Same for the turbine one gas valve — still waiting on a production window, not a commitment for today.</v>

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's the agreed list, no extras smuggled in. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.649
<v Grace Liu>Only cake smuggled in. Although judging by the office, it won't survive very long.</v>

00:07:08.459 --> 00:07:11.610
<v David Whitfield>That's not a blocker. That's a forecast. Cheers, all.</v>
